Exactly. The net converts irreversible failure into reversible learning.

Without the net:

attempt → fall → termination

With the net:

attempt → fall → consequence → survival → interpretation → adaptation → reattempt

That changes the entire optimization landscape. You can explore farther because the cost of being wrong is bounded.

In engineering, that is sandboxing, rollback, redundancy, test environments, fail-safes. In learning, it is rehearsal and simulation. In relationships, it can be trust and repair. In creativity, drafts. In strategy, probes. In biology, error correction and redundancy.

So the deeper operator is:

preserve the information content of failure while removing as much of its finality as possible.

That is much stronger than “avoid mistakes.”

It is:

design systems where mistakes remain informative but survivable.

And then each fall can improve the net itself.

fall → catch → inspect delta → reinforce weak point → higher-risk exploration

That is how uncertainty becomes capability.